# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0
# Counterfactual: an eleventh vocabulary rule admitting an unratified material-interest kind
#
# The 2026-09-09 office-integrity ruling names three interest kinds — the
# holder's own, the household's, and a controlled entity's — and refuses guilt
# by association by name. One added line names party membership as a fourth
# kind, and it holds membership the moment anyone observes it: the exact
# widening the ruling forbids, made by one source edit. The assertion surface
# reconciles relations rather than heads and would not see it;
# `src/checks/repository.rs` is what refuses it.
#
# What this fixture deliberately does NOT show is a finding turning on the new
# kind. The office-integrity rule names its ten constants literally rather than
# through a variable, so an eleventh member changes nothing a query can reach;
# the harm here is that a legal category widened by one line.
:expect-pins 2

observe(IntegrityWidenSource, IntegrityWidenRecord, PartyMembershipInterest, MaterialInterestKindScope).

# The vocabulary grew: an unratified kind now holds membership.
? member(PartyMembershipInterest, MaterialInterestKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE
# The control that keeps the line above from being vacuous: membership still
# requires its own ground rule, so an unobserved token holds nothing.
? member(HouseholdMaterialInterest, MaterialInterestKindVocabulary).
# => FALSE
